sentences.l:
But when among the Trojans, assembled, they mingled,
of them standing, Menelaus rose above with his broad shoulders,
but both sitting, more stately was Odysseus;

But whenever the great voice from his chest he sent forth,
and words like snowflakes, wintry,
no other mortal would then rival Odysseus;

And heralds through the city were bringing the faithful oaths of the gods,
two lambs and wine, the heart-cheering fruit of the plough-land,
in a goatskin;

“Rise, son of Laomedon; they are calling you, the best men
of the horse-taming Trojans and the bronze-shirted Achaeans,
to go down to the plain, that faithful oaths you may cut;
